<section class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Meet Ben</p>
    <h1>Technical depth, product judgment, and a bias toward useful work.</h1>
    <p>Ben Dewey is an independent product and technology leader based in Charleston, South Carolina. He is seeking his next leadership opportunity and is available for select advisory work.</p>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
    <h2>A career built by making complex work clearer.</h2>
    <p>Ben started as a hands-on application developer, sharing what he learned through writing, books, open-source work, and conference talks. That foundation grew into leading product, user experience, and delivery teams across enterprise and public-sector work.</p>
    <p>His experience includes technology transformation, product strategy, service and experience design, and the practical work of helping teams turn an idea into something people can use. Most recently, he led large teams at EY. Earlier chapters include technical community leadership, published technical books, and founder work through Nuology.</p>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
    <h2>How Ben works</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Start with the people, decisions, and outcomes that make the work matter.</li>
        <li>Connect product, design, technology, and delivery around a shared direction.</li>
        <li>Build momentum through clear priorities, honest communication, and practical iteration.</li>
    </ul>
</section>
